The game design document should be adjusted as plans and needs for the project change. 
It should exist in the form of something like a google doc, shared among the team members with multiple people allowed to view and edit it. 

For my team's game design document, we'll use hacknplan. 
Hacknplan lets us set tasks and the items the tasks are associated with and assign those tasks to people by connecting it to their profiles. 
Every week, my team will meet to discuss the project and make adjustments to the game design document. 
The point of these meetings is to keep the team on task and make sure the scope of the project stays manageable.
If a direction we had planned on for a feature proves too time consuming, we can change direction for a compromise 
that accomplishes the same feeling without taking too much time and effecting the rest of the project.
